  "text": "Skip to content\nSoren Hale\n01\nWork\n02\nServices\n03\nAbout\n04\nLab\n05\nWriting\nOpen to work from November\nGet in touch\n~\nWork\nLedgerline Console\n\n// Case study\n\nLedgerline Console \n\nForty internal tools moved into one console, on one design system, with one way to ship.\n\nRead the code\n\nFrom merge to production\nfrom\n14 min\n→\nto\n95 s\n\nClient\nLedgerline\nYear\n2024\nRole\nFrontend architect\nKind\nTooling\n01\nThe problem\n\nLedgerline's operations teams worked in forty separate tools, each with its own login, its own table component and its own idea of a date picker.\n\n02\nThe approach\nOne shell that owns routing, auth and layout; each team ships its own module into it.\nA shared component library with typed props and visual tests on every pull request.\nA build that only rebuilds what a change touches.\nA developer at two monitors at night with city lights behind\nA desk lamp and a closed notebook against a blue city dusk\n03\nThe result\n\nA merge now reaches production in 95 seconds instead of 14 minutes. New tools start from a template and are usable on day two. Six teams deleted their private UI kits within the quarter.\n\nBuilt with\n\nReact\nTypeScript\nModule Federation\nTurborepo\n\nNext case\nProduct · 2024\nKestrel Pay Dashboard\nLive payment data on a table of 200,000 rows that still answers a click at once.\n\n// Start a project\n\nTell me what you are building. \n\nThree quick picks so the first reply is useful. You finish the message on the contact page.\n\n01\nWhat do you need?\n\nFrontend build\nPerformance audit\nDesign system\nTeam embed\nSomething else\n\n02\nRough budget\n\nUnder €5k\n€5–10k\n€10–25k\n€25k+\nNot sure yet\n03\nYour name or company\nbrief.ts\ndraft, not sent\nexport const brief = {\nkind: null // not picked yet,\nbudget: null // not picked yet,\nname: null // not picked yet,\n}\n\nBrief so far: nothing picked yet\n\nContinue to contact\n\nor write to hello@sorenhale.dev\n\nNothing is sent from this page. Your picks are kept in this browser tab and wait for you on the contact form.\n\nFooter\n\nFrontend developer, Oslo\n\nWrite to me\nhello@sorenhale.dev\n\nOpen to work from November\n\n// Site\n\nWork\nServices\nProcess\nReviews\nContact\n\n// About\n\nAbout\nResume\nStack\nUses\nNow\n\n// More\n\nLab\nWriting\nFAQ\nPrivacy\nTerms\nCookies\n\n// Elsewhere\n\nGitHub\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nLinkedIn\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nBluesky\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\n\nLocal time, Oslo\n17:01 CEST\n\n© 2026 Soren Hale. Written by hand in Oslo.\n\nSorenHale\n\nCreate a free website with Framer, the website builder loved by startups, designers and agencies.\n\nEdit Content",
